use "@std"

Note: DX-06 flat-letter family inside note streams (extended NoteType.Parse surface)
Sequence flats = | Db4 Eb4 Gb4 Ab4 Bb4 Cb4 Fb4 |
(print (str flats))

Note: DX-06 bare flats default to octave 4 (no octave digit required)
Sequence bare = | Bb Db Eb |
(print (str bare))

Note: DX-06 sharp-hash equivalence in note streams
Sequence sharps = | C#4 F##4 G#5 |
(print (str sharps))

Note: DX-06 post-octave alteration runs (absorbed by SimpleLexer alteration pickup)
Note: Full mixed pre+post composition like "Bb-+bbb" and "C+5++" is covered by unit
Note: Facts (NoteTypeTests.Parse_MixedAlteration / Parse_PreOctaveAndPostOctave). In
Note: note-stream syntax, '+' and '-' are token boundaries, so the end-to-end surface
Note: is: letter + (b|#)* + digits + (+|-)* within a single identifier.
Sequence posts = | Bb4-- F#4+ D4- |
(print (str posts))

